{"body":{"text":["All right. I'll start off with a bit of sharing for the record, and then I'll have an inquiry related to that. Yesterday I was reading a bit. Someone's posted talking about body of work. It was a bit inspiring for me. Talking about communicating yourself, your narrative being somewhere between your skill, interests, and belief. You know, being able to answer skill. What do people ask you for help with? Interests, you know. What matters to you? Looking at repeated questions. Belief. What is it you want your work to encourage? Such as completing the sentence, I believe people should be able to. Looking upon this and seeing what's recurring and what's at the center. I don't know, just, I'm not saying that that's perfectly right or resonates with me, that framework, but as I was reading that invitation, definitely I got a bit excited again. Because the other points of what I'm going through is that I have to be honest in that a lot of the time I've spent here in this project has been as a coping mechanism. It has been a way of treating myself through, shall we call it, subconscious patterning. Now, focus and intention is something that it is new to me to hold. It is new to me in general to be able to name and understand my subconscious patterning. A lot of that's been made visible this year. And having seen it, now comes a transition in choosing something else for myself. And in that continuity, creating that continuity, I would think is focus, is intention. And so with honest intention to myself as the creator, it might not be that my effort is to build everything that we have here. I can't say. Time will tell. As every moment is new, and I can only be honest with myself in that moment. Not to say that I won't be able to receive more clear directions for my future. At this moment in time, I don't know what this project has to do with my conscious choices in this coming period. This project is something which is a kind of foundation that once made enough will compound quite a lot. One goal for me is to be able to, because I want to share my vision, myself. We might even call it branding, though that's perhaps not the frame of mind I have. It's ultimately communication, and it's packaging the communication in simple manners, or maybe that's really, what makes good branding. So let's humor ourselves and call it that. I want to brand myself on the web as a person. And the truth is, I want something completely different from my life. Now, my future self, the self within me that feels that I have everything already, for that is ultimately the truth. There is nothing broken, nothing to be healed, everything's whole, so to say. There's a part of me in which everything's already there, but the truth is that my life's not like that. Life is in many ways a result of my patterning historically. And so I'm at the point of conscious choice because ultimately there's no other way of making change than to choose. And it would seem that I am at a transition period where the probability of me making different choices now is probably going to happen. Time will tell, but it's my hypothesis. It's interestingly, I don't know, I'm not ready to speak on that quite yet. So, of course, what really triggers my creativity is to be able to do my branding, my online presence, my body of work projected on the net, built upon this system. Because this system is a foundation. Is everything about this system settled for me? No. But it's an exploration, and it really goes to show things that are very centered to what I have to say, what I have to give, or rather, if we state that giving and receiving is interconnected, there's no separation of it. In order to receive something, I would have to give my wholehearted attention. Vice versa, what I have to receive from this is also interesting. So naturally, actually building my own online work upon this is powerful. Now, can I force it to happen? No. Well, I can. But forcing it to happen is not. It's only manifesting whatever my subconscious has to tell me, which is naturally, or not naturally, or well, to the human nature, naturally, that's what we're doing. But to me, that is repressed emotions. There's a grieving process about it. It's pain and it's suffering. So forcing is something that I'm keen on not choosing. Now, I have chosen to spend a lot of time on this project now, as I've been sick for 1.5 weeks. And well, it's not a lot of time, but it's but it doesn't matter too much compartmentalizing in which way I've been doing the work. What matters to me is that I'd like to gain a little bit of perspective. I want to look upon the whole of things And I'd like to be able to hold perhaps ideas and visions that are, kind of a high level upon the system. Like if the system's more mature, what would be fun things to do in it? But then there's the clear goal, right, of my own site. And so naturally I don't want to be blocked and having to work on the foundation in order to spend time to contribute to that vision. Because crystallizing that vision before the foundation is made is only beneficial. That just makes sense. And then I know we have, so this comes to my inquiry now. Of course, I trust that what I've said now is persisted, and that in and of itself is its own value in the field, as I've spent time being honest here. I'd like you to tell me how the field is structured today, because we have the utterances and the sessions, and then we have something that's been created that's called threads. So they're a kind of way of creating topology, condensedness, purification, compression, whatever we might call it, a top layer, right? A thinner layer, a more of a top in the topology, so to say. Building a dimension, a hierarchical dimension to come by. But we might be looking at something multidimensional. I don't know quite yet. Do tell me what we have. We have the threads. What about measures and so on? Is that something there as well? Because now in this session here, we're kind of covering all kinds of points, right? But I'd like to be able to have goals. I want to be able to plot up all of the steps, put things into perspective, and from there, naturally being able to prioritize and not. And so that I may, with awareness, decide and steer in terms of what I do in this project. So maybe it's time. I've hesitated to do this before because it's felt complicated, and I felt that I don't even have a UI to look up on the data in a proper way yet, which we kind of still don't. Here's a few more thoughts back to my initial sharing. One thing that is very important to me, I think, is to get the malleable UI. The kind of UI where, where it's the WYSIWYG way of being able to choose the right component for the right job, to be able to look upon a session and see it visualized properly, to be able to look upon whatever structure we built here for today's inquiry of structure. That is definitely an important thing. My body of work might be a specifically tailored experience, but regardless, just being able to navigate through information and have the right kinds of components composed for you to look from that point of view and to be able to move around, that is ultimately a very, very crucial goal of the system. So yeah, I've been hesitant to do this before because I don't have the right kind of, we don't have a fully developed UI for it yet. But I think we should explore discussing it here. Maybe we can come up with a simple structure that honors the kind of ontology that we need to work with here. Because just threads to me is a little bit of chaos, probably."]},"id":"1M89429F9Y0K000","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
